    "md5": "d0f4e3b7ea9846b95c30305c6aed00fc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1831,
    "chunk_text": "CSE picks-up speed following CBSL interest rate decision and growth predictions\n\nCSE trading activities took off at a slow pace yesterday but later turned positive following the Central Bank\u2019s decision to keep policy rates unchanged at 7.75 percent and projections that the decision will help in steering inflation towards the target of 5 percent coupled with an expansion of economic growth, market analysts said.\n\nAmid those developments both indices moved upwards. The All Share Price Index went up by 55.6 points while S and P SL20 rose by 14.08 points. Turnover stood at Rs 5.57 billion with 12 crossings. The top seven crossings were: VallibelOne 3.6 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 372 million and its shares traded at Rs 103, Jetwing Symphony 13 million shares crossed for Rs 227 million; its shares traded at Rs 18.10, Hayleys 700,000 shares crossed for Rs 130 million; its shares traded at Rs 188.\n\nCeylinco Holdings 30000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 95.2 million; its shares traded at Rs 3175, DFCC 500,000 shares crossed for Rs 81.4 million; its shares traded at Rs 162.75, Commercial Bank 392,000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 76 million; its shares traded at Rs 194 and HNB (Non- Voting) 150,000 shares crossed for Rs 44.8 million; its shares traded at Rs 299.\n\nIn the retail market companies that mainly contributed to the turnover were; Browns Investments Rs 307 million (37.8 million shares traded), LB Finance Rs 219 million (1.5 million shares traded), JKH Rs 212 million (9.4 million shares traded), NTB Rs 211 million (669,000 shares traded), Vallibel One Rs 186 million (1.8 million shares traded), PickMe Rs 166 million (1.2 million shares traded) and Sierra Cables Rs 160 million (5.7 million shares traded). During the day 185.8 million share volumes changed hands in 31214 transactions."
