    "md5": "a0919ef42bfb43b199815a2cc87f1c82",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1862,
    "chunk_text": "ComBank wins impressive triple at ICC Emerging Asia Banking Conclave & Awards 2025\n\nThe Commercial Bank of Ceylon was honoured with three prestigious awards at the 3rd Emerging Asia Banking Conclave & Awards 2025, organised by the Indian Chamber of Commerce (ICC).\n\nThe Bank received the awards for Best Performance on Growth \u2013 Sri Lanka and Best Performance on Profitability \u2013 Sri Lanka, and won the Runner-up title for Best Bank in Sri Lanka, achieving a significant triple at this event.\n\nThese accolades, presented at Le Meridien in New Delhi, India, highlight the Bank\u2019s robust performance, resilience, and leadership within the region\u2019s financial sector.\n\nRepresenting the Bank at the event was Mr. Ramachandren Sivagnanam, the Assistant General Manager \u2013 Personal Banking. The awards ceremony featured participation from financial institutions across Bhutan, Sri Lanka, Nepal, Myanmar, Bangladesh, and India.\n\nCommenting on the recognition, the Bank said this distinguished recognition serves as a powerful validation of the Bank\u2019s unwavering commitment to its customer-centric strategies, continuous innovation, and financial strength. These accolades not only reinforce trust and differentiate the Bank in a highly competitive market but also strengthen its reputation among customers, employees, and all stakeholders.\n\nThe awards are based on a rigorous assessment conduct by PricewaterhouseCoopers (PwC) and a jury of eminent banking industry professionals, which considers both quantitative and qualitative factors, including key financial indicators such as profitability, growth, and asset quality.\n\nFounded in 1925 and headquartered in Kolkata, the Indian Chamber of Commerce is one of the most proactive and forward-looking Chambers in India today. Its membership spans some of the most prominent and major industrial groups in India."
