    "chunk_text": "The ongoing investigation into the Easter Sunday attacks is widely considered emblematic because it is expected to delve into a host of crucial issues, such as systemic failures in intelligence and the State\u2019s inability to ensure expeditious delivery of justice. Several negative factors have taken their toll on the current probe, the main being a conflict of interest.\n\nA presidential committee has held Seneviratne and Abeysekera accountable for the CID\u2019s failure to prevent the 2019 carnage and recommended legal action against them. The NPP government has dismissed the committee report as baseless, but the fact remains that the CID, under the duo\u2019s watch, failed to prevent the terror strikes, and the possibility of a future government instituting legal action against them cannot be ruled out. Abeysekera\u2019s subservience to the Yahapalana politicians severely compromised his credibility. An audio clip of a conversation between him and the then Deputy Minister Ranjan Ramanayake is a case in point. In 2023, Seneviratne was prosecuted for causing a road accident under the influence of alcohol. The Opposition says the drunk driving charge against him has now been withdrawn! So, his critics argue that his interests will be safeguarded in a similar manner as regards the CID\u2019s failure to prevent the Easter Sunday terror attacks."
