    "date_str": "2025-09-25",
    "description": "President Anura Kumara urges world leaders to commit themselves to building a safe world for future generations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.adaderana.lk/news/112887/president-anura-kumara-urges-world-leaders-to-commit-themselves-to-building-a-safe-world-for-future-generations",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "adaderanalk",
    "time_ut": 1758755280.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-09-25-adaderanalk-c7c6b77a-0005",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "99ca789ca7b3723ad541da672dddef1b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1983,
    "chunk_text": "Opportunistic power politics has turned the lives of children and innocent civilians into a game. No one has the right to inflict pain and suffering on another to enhance one\u2019s own power. The duty of a ruler is not to destroy lives but to protect them.\n\nWe also believe that legal, security and humanitarian concerns of Israel and Palestinian people need to be acknowledged.\n\nSri Lanka reiterates the importance of early implementation of the UN General Assembly resolutions regarding a two-state solution on the basis of the 1967 borders. The time has come for the international community to stop being a mere spectator and to move decisively to end the suffering of millions.\n\nReligious extremism and racism have been major causes of wars and conflicts, bringing suffering to millions of people.\n\nAlthough a century has passed since the abolition of slavery, the poison of racism still lingers in many places. Extremist and racist ideas are as deadly as epidemics. We must ask ourselves how these extremist and racist ideas survive like sparks under the ashes in a world that has witnessed so many advances on so many fronts.\n\nI believe that we must awaken our conscience to oppose racism and religious extremism in protection of human rights and freedoms. We must be brave enough to speak up for peace. We must not be afraid to speak up against war. We must be afraid to speak up for war. In a world where millions of children die of hunger, we spend millions on weapons. When tens of millions die of inadequate health facilities, hundreds of millions are spent on futile wars. When hundreds of thousands of children are denied the right to an education, millions are spent on invading another\u2019s land.\n\nIf every inch of this world can be turned into peaceful communities, what a wonderful world would it be. As a country that suffered the horrors of war for decades, where families still weep in remembrance of their loved ones, we have a duty to make that heartfelt proposal."
  },
  {
