    "md5": "552f131f66503afeb1e9d4d4b7d39d56",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1860,
    "chunk_text": "IASL hosts 16th NAFLIA Conference, driving growth\n\nThe Insurance Association of Sri Lanka (IASL), through its Marketing and Sales Forum, hosted the 16th consecutive NAFLIA Conference at the Monarch Imperial. This landmark event continues to play a critical role in developing and recognising the professionalism of life insurance advisors in the country, reaffirming IASL\u2019s ongoing commitment to elevating industry standards and upholding excellence within the life insurance sector.\n\nThis year\u2019s conference was held under the theme \u201cDrivers of Change: Driving Growth in a New World of Insurance.\u201d The event focused on the evolving role of life insurance advisors in a rapidly transforming industry landscape strengthened by technological advancement, shifting customer expectations, demographic changes, regulatory reforms and dynamic market trends. It was emphasized that agents must move beyond adaptation to lead transformative change, proactively embracing innovation, upskilling digitally and delivering customer-centric solutions to build trust and long-term impact.\n\nOver 700 attendees participated in the event, including representatives from the Insurance Regulatory Commission of Sri Lanka (IRCSL), members of IASL, CEOs of leading insurance companies, advisors, team members and other key stakeholders in the industry. The conference created a valuable platform for sharing insights, exploring challenges and collectively shaping the future of life insurance in Sri Lanka.\n\nAmong the highlights of the event was the keynote speech delivered by Director of the Postgraduate Institute of Management (PIM) and Chairman, Dr. Asanga Ranasinghe, who shared thought-provoking perspectives on the opportunities presented in the sector with dynamic demographic and technological changes, demanding leadership, growth and transformation in the space."
  },
