    "md5": "d68e11aa1cc638a96fe5aa2105f7e9d5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1688,
    "chunk_text": "APIDM launches AI Proficiency for Business Professionals Program\n\nThe Asia Pacific Institute of Digital Marketing (APIDM) officially launched its groundbreaking AI Proficiency for Business Professionals Program at BMICH, Colombo. This initiative marks a milestone in Sri Lanka\u2019s digital transformation journey, empowering leaders, executives, and entrepreneurs to harness AI for business growth, innovation, and responsible leadership.\n\nUnlike technical AI courses, this program is designed to bridge the gap between artificial intelligence and business decision-making, equipping professionals with practical skills to integrate AI into strategy, operations, and day-to-day workflows. It is tailored for non-technical professionals, giving them the confidence and capability to lead AI-driven change within their organizations.\n\nThe program has been developed with clear objectives: to equip professionals with a strong understanding of AI concepts and trends, enable effective decision-making through AI-driven insights, enhance productivity and efficiency with AI-powered tools, foster innovation to address business challenges, and ultimately create future-ready leaders who can guide organizations in the AI era.\n\nAdding perspective, Amitha Amarasinghe, Co-founder and CEO of APIDM, said: \u201cAt APIDM, our mission has always been to prepare professionals for the future of work. With the launch of this program, we are taking the next big step, enabling Sri Lanka\u2019s workforce to thrive in an AI-driven economy. This initiative is not just about technology adoption; it\u2019s about creating future-ready leaders who can drive meaningful transformation for businesses and society.\u201d"
