    "md5": "2772e69546873056cbcff3320cae7e16",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 944,
    "chunk_text": "Sarkozy\u2019s Conviction\n\nThe wheels of justice apparently turn slowly across the globe. French President Nicolas Sarkozy, 70, was yesterday found guilty of criminal conspiracy in a high-profile trial wherein he and his top aides were accused of having struck a corrupt deal with the late Libyan dictator Muammar Gaddafi to secure funding for the 2007 presidential election. Sarkozy was acquitted of three charges. Sentencing had not been announced at the time of going to press, and Sarkozy was expected to appeal immediately.\n\nA criminal probe got underway against Sarkozy in 2013 following a much-publicised claim by Gaddafi\u2019s son, Saif al-Islam that Sarkozy had benefited from the Libyan dictator\u2019s largesse in the 2007 presidential election. The French prosecutors argued that Sarkozy had received funds from Gaddafi to help repair the latter\u2019s image internationally, especially in the West, which had conferred pariah status on Libya."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-25-islandlk-4220f7dc",
