    "chunk_size_bytes": 1144,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka rupee weaker against dollar, bond yields steady\n\nECONOMYNEXT \u2013 Sri Lanka\u2019s rupee opened at 302.60/63 to the US dollar on Friday, weaker from 302.50/55 the previous day, while bond yields were broadly steady, dealers said.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.12.2026 was quoted at 8.25/30 percent, down from 8.25/32 percent.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.09.2027 was quoted at 8.70/80 percent, down from 8.70/82 percent.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.12.2028 was quoted flat at 9.10/15 percent.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.12.2029 was quoted at 9.50/60 percent, up from 9.52/56 percent.\n\nA bond maturing on 01.07.2030 was quoted flat at 9.70/75 percent, from 9.70/75 percent.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.12.2032 was quoted at 10.45/50 percent, up from 10.43/47 percent.\n\nThe telegraphic transfer rates for the American dollar was 299.0000 buying, 306.0000 selling; the British pound was 397.8953 buying, and 409.2571 selling, and the euro was 346.5991 buying, 357.9623 selling.\n\nThe Colombo Stocks Exchange was trading in green; The ASPI was up 0.16 percent, or 34.59 points, at 21,555; the S&P SL20 was up 0.08 percent, or 5.16 points, at 6,107. (Colombo/Sep26/2025)."
  },
