    "chunk_text": "Bourse\u2019s robustness boosted by LB Finance\u2019s acquisition of 55.6% stake in Associated Motorways\n\nStock market activities continued with their positive proclivities yesterday and a transaction of note was the acquisition of a 55.6 percent stake in Association Motorways Pvt. Ltd by LB Finance. Under this acquisition, LB Finance invested Rs 3.7 billion to purchase 74.3 million shares at a share price of Rs 50. This enabled to increase the business portfolio to a great extent of LB Finance, market analysts said.\n\nAmid those developments both indices moved upwards. The All Share Price Index went up by 77.93 points, while the S and P SL20 rose by 10.95 points. Turnover stood at Rs 6 billion with nine crossings.\n\nThose crossings were; Commercial Bank 1.5 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 291.5 million; its shares traded at Rs 193.50, LOLC Holdings 95000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 55.5 million; its shares sold at Rs 580, Hemas Holdings 1.6 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 52.9 million; its shares traded at Rs 33, HNB (Non- Voting) 168,000 shares crossed for Rs 49.9 million and its shares traded at Rs 297.\n\nJKH 1.4 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 31.6 million; its shares traded at Rs 22, Sunshine Holdings one million shares crossed for Rs 31 million; its shares sold at Rs 31, CIC Holdings (Non- Voting) 200,000 shares crossed for Rs 24.6 million; its shares sold at Rs 123, Sanasa Developments Bank 500,000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 23.5 million; its shares sold traded at Rs 47 and Melstacope 125,000 shares crossed for Rs 20.8 million; its shares traded at Rs 157."
