    "md5": "34de39eccffa6eca20ce74b510f41275",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1263,
    "chunk_text": "Siyapatha Finance launches national school-level tree planting project marking two decades of growth\n\nEmbodying two decades of growth and perseverance from its modest roots to service excellence, Siyapatha Finance PLC launched an islandwide school-level tree planting project and art competition in 20 schools across 13 regions.\n\nEach participating school planted 20 Mee trees (Mahua longifolia) representing the company\u2019s 20-year-long journey in the financial services industry.\n\nSiyapatha Finance PLC Managing Director Ananda Seneviratne noted: \u201cAs we celebrate our 20th anniversary, we are pleased to launch this school-level tree planting project as a gesture of our gratitude to the environment. We need to constantly acknowledge that trees and nature are not only central to the survival of all living beings but vital for a sustainable future. And this project goes beyond merely planting trees \u2013 it is about bringing young minds together and empowering them to embrace the power nature holds in all of our lives.\u201d\n\nThe art competition at the event opened an avenue for young talent to express their connection to nature through creativity. Each school selected 20 winners and distributed backpacks and certificates in recognition of their efforts."
