    "chunk_text": "Across the world, schools and universities are showing how education can drive sustainability. In Denmark, the Green School Flag program involves over 1,400 schools in projects that have measurably cut waste. Brazil\u2019s Sustainable Schools Program establishes schools as central hubs for sustainability and to support local economies. In Asia-Pacific, Japan\u2019s education system embeds Mottainai \u2013 a philosophy of respect for resources \u2013 into its curriculum. Singapore\u2019s Food Waste Prevention Programme combines lessons with practical campaigns, with over 80% of participating households reporting reduced waste. Universities like Arizona State, Stanford, and Wageningen have created \u201cliving labs,\u201d where students design and test circular solutions, some achieving near zero-waste campuses.\n\nComplementing these efforts, FAO\u2019s Do Good: Save Food materials \u2013 available in Tamil, Sinhala, and many other languages \u2013 provide children, teachers, and families with simple, practical ways to reduce food waste in daily life. By making these practices accessible and actionable, the resources empower communities to contribute meaningfully to the global movement to save food and protect the planet."
