    "chunk_size_bytes": 1988,
    "chunk_text": "CSE Masterminds Quiz offers over Rs. 3.5 million in prizes for its 7th edition\n\nThe Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE) announces the seventh edition of the CSE Masterminds Quiz on 17th October 2025 from 3.00 p.m. onwards at the Main Ballroom, Shangri-La Colombo.\n\nRecognized as Sri Lanka\u2019s premier capital market quiz competition, the event will bring together teams from the public and private sector to compete for glory in six subject areas, in international business, global markets, Sri Lankan economy and business, local capital market, sports & entertainment, and current affairs.\n\nThis year\u2019s competition will offer prizes worth over Rs. 3.5 million. The champion team will walk away with Rs. 1,000,000/-, while the second and third-placed teams will receive Rs. 500,000/- and Rs. 375,000/-, respectively.\n\nIn addition, the winning teams of the first three places will have the opportunity to double their prize money, provided that all team members hold CDS accounts with at least one transaction completed during 2025. Sector prizes will also be awarded to the best-performing teams representing each sector.\n\nPlatinum Sponsors: SC Securities (Pvt) Ltd. and Almas Equities (Pvt) Ltd.\n\nGold Sponsors: Ex-Pack Corrugated Cartons PLC, Bartleet Religare Securities (Pvt) Ltd., NDB Capital Holdings (Pvt) Ltd. and TWC Capital (Pvt) Ltd.\n\nSilver Sponsors: Asha Securities Ltd., Lanka Securities (Pvt) Ltd., Softlogic Stockbrokers (Pvt) Ltd., Nestor Stock Brokers (Pvt) Ltd., and LOLC Holdings PLC.\n\nShangri-La Colombo will serve as the Official Hospitality Partner, FitsAir (Pvt) Ltd. as the Official Airline Partner, and Co-sponsors including Sarvodaya Development Finance PLC, CT Smith Holdings Ltd., People\u2019s Leasing & Finance PLC, Alliance Finance Company PLC, Capital Trust Holdings (Pvt) Ltd., Barista Coffee Lanka (Pvt) Ltd., Crypto Gen (Pvt) Ltd., Hemas Holding PLC and Teejay Lanka PLC.\n\nThe event\u2019s print media partners include Daily FT, Daily Mirror and the Sunday Times."
