    "chunk_size_bytes": 1296,
    "chunk_text": "The Sri Lanka\u2013Japan Business Council leads successful delegation to Japan\n\nThe Sri Lanka\u2013Japan Business Council of the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce successfully led a high-level business delegation to Japan in September 2025, coinciding with the official visit of Anura Kumara Dissanayake, President of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka.\n\nThe delegation, led by Krishan Balendra, Chairperson of the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce, with Mr. Kariyawasam, Immediate Past President, playing a pivotal role, attended the Sri Lanka Business Forum in Tokyo, organized and co-organized by the Japan External Trade Organization (JETRO), the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry (METI), the Japan\u2013Sri Lanka Business Cooperation Committee, and the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka (BOI), with support from the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA).\n\nThe delegation also had the honor of attending a dinner hosted by the Japan Business Council, participating in the Sri Lanka Business Forum and Networking Session organized by the Export Development Board (EDB) in Osaka, and taking part in the Japan Expo, further strengthening bilateral business linkages.\n\nThe delegation\u2019s efforts were supported by the Sri Lankan Embassy in Japan, including the Ambassador of Sri Lanka to Japan."
