    "chunk_text": "ASPI exceeds 22,000 point mark as bourse\u2019s bullish exuberance continues\n\nCSE activities continued with their bullish exuberance yesterday when the IMF made positive observations on the Sri Lankan economy at an on line media conference. Subsequent positive economic indicators were attributed to this upward trend, such as the ASPI going beyond the 22,000 point mark.\n\nBesides the S&P SL20 index, which tracks the top 20 largest and most liquid stocks on the stock market, crossed 6,200 points during trading hours.\n\nThe stock market hit a new record in the first half hour of trading when the All Share Price Index went beyond the 22,000 points mark.\n\nThe All Share Price Index went up by 143 points, while the S and P SL20 rose by 41.4 points. Turnover stood at Rs 9.7 billion with 17 crossings.\n\nTop seven crossings were; Lanka Credit and Business, 135 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 878 million and its shares traded at Rs 6.50, Commercial Bank 2.95 million shares crossed for Rs 572 million and its shares traded at Rs 194, DFCC 1.1 million shares crossed for Rs 185.9 million and its shares traded at Rs 164, Sanasa Developments Bank 3.2 million shares crossed for Rs 158 million; its shares traded at Rs 50, Dipped Products 1.78 million shares crossed for Rs 125 million; its shares sold at Rs 70. Pan Asia Bank 1.5 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 98.5 million; its shares sold at Rs 66 and Distilleries 1.5 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 90 million; its shares traded at Rs 60."
